---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const focusAreas = [
  {
    title: 'Embedded Systems',
    description: 'Understanding the full stack from hardware peripherals to application-level firmware.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Microcontrollers',
    description: 'Working with ARM Cortex-M (STM32) and ESP32 architectures, peripherals, and datasheets.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Electronics Design-PCB Engineering',
    description: 'Schematic capture, PCB layout, and component selection using KiCad and Altium.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Firmware Development',
    description: 'Writing efficient, reliable C code for resource-constrained devices and real-time systems.',
  },
  {
    title: 'IoT & Edge AI',
    description: 'Connecting embedded devices to the cloud and exploring on-device machine learning with TinyML.',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="About — Shiva Dulam"
  description="About Shiva Dulam — an Electronics, Embedded Systems & PCB Engineer building a foundation in microcontroller architecture, firmware development, PCB design, and IoT, with a structured learning path from circuit fundamentals to system-level design."
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Background, focus, and where I'm headed.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>
      I'm Shiva Dulam, an Electronics, Embedded Systems & PCB Engineer in the early stage of my
      career. My interest lies in the intersection of hardware and software — how a circuit board
      becomes a useful device once the right firmware runs on it.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm currently dedicating my time to building a strong foundation through hands-on projects,
      datasheet study, and coursework covering microcontroller architecture, real-time systems, and
      printed circuit board design.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Current Focus Areas</h2>
    <div class="focus-grid">
      {focusAreas.map((area) => (
        <div class="focus-card">
          <h3>{area.title}</h3>
          <p>{area.description}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Learning Journey & Goals</h2>
    <p>
      I'm taking a structured approach to building my expertise — starting with the fundamentals of
      digital and analog electronics, then moving into microcontroller programming and peripheral
      interfacing, and finally tackling system-level design with real-time operating systems and
      custom PCBs.
    </p>
    <p>
      Over the next two to three years, my goal is to move from learning exercises to complete,
      deployable embedded systems. I want to design boards that solve real problems, write firmware
      that is robust and maintainable, and develop a portfolio that demonstrates both depth and
      breadth across the embedded stack.
    </p>
    <p>
      Alongside hands-on practice, I've been building a structured foundation through self-paced
      coursework — MIT's 6.002 (Circuits and Electronics) and Electronics-Tutorials.ws for core
      electronics, Neso Academy for digital electronics and C programming, and CS50 and Jacob
      Sorber's content for programming fundamentals.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .focus-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .focus-card {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 22px;
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.25s ease;
  }

  .focus-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent-border);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--accent-border), 0 4px 20px rgba(126, 160, 204, 0.08);
  }

  .focus-card h3 {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .focus-card p {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .focus-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
